    <md:title>6.1.5: Reviewing Polynomial Addition and Subtraction</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d1f8c81f-0f50-4add-88d7-91ce295ed497</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title> Student Activity</title>
<para>Draw a tic-tac-toe board on an extra sheet of paper. Use the polynomial functions shown here for the activity.</para>
<para>\(f(x) = 8x^2-6x-2\)</para>
<para>For each polynomial problem below, place an \(X\) on your tic-tac-toe board corresponding to the location of its matching solution.</para>
<para>\(16x^2-9x^2 =\) ________</para>
<para>For each polynomial problem below, place an \(O\) on your tic-tac-toe board corresponding to the location of its matching solution.</para>
<para>\(11x^3+12x^3 =\) ________</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e310d0a16f3d61f97baba81e24833db21176e58c"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Did the \(Xs\) or \(Os\) win the tic-tac-toe game?</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The \(Xs\) won the game.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0556198676e4a9a50149f1b5370bdc40d0a2dd91"/></media></figure></para>
<para><emphasis>Xs:</emphasis></para>
<para>\(16x^2-9x^2 = 7x^2\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Os:</emphasis></para>
<para>\(11x^3+12x^3 = 23x^3\)</para></section>
